(go/type Value "Value is the reflection interface to a Go value.\n\nNot all methods apply to all kinds of values. Restrictions,\nif any, are noted in the documentation for each method.\nUse the Kind method to find out the kind of value before\ncalling kind-specific methods. Calling a method\ninappropriate to the kind of type causes a run time panic.\n\nThe zero Value represents no value.\nIts IsValid method returns false, its Kind method returns Invalid,\nits String method returns \"<invalid Value>\", and all other methods panic.\nMost functions and methods never return an invalid value.\nIf one does, its documentation states the conditions explicitly.\n\nA Value can be used concurrently by multiple goroutines provided that\nthe underlying Go value can be used concurrently for the equivalent\ndirect operations.\n\nTo compare two Values, compare the results of the Interface method.\nUsing == on two Values does not compare the underlying values\nthey represent.\n" (struct


    ^{:line 39 :tag (* abi/Type) :doc "typ_ holds the type of the value represented by a Value.\nAccess using the typ method to avoid escape of v.\n"} typ_



    ^{:line 43 :tag unsafe/Pointer :doc "Pointer-valued data or, if flagIndir is set, pointer to data.\nValid when either flagIndir is set or typ.pointers() is true.\n"} ptr















    ^{:line 59 :doc "flag holds metadata about the value.\n\nThe lowest five bits give the Kind of the value, mirroring typ.Kind().\n\nThe next set of bits are flag bits:\n\t- flagStickyRO: obtained via unexported not embedded field, so read-only\n\t- flagEmbedRO: obtained via unexported embedded field, so read-only\n\t- flagIndir: val holds a pointer to the data\n\t- flagAddr: v.CanAddr is true (implies flagIndir and ptr is non-nil)\n\t- flagMethod: v is a method value.\nIf !typ.IsDirectIface(), code can assume that flagIndir is set.\n\nThe remaining 22+ bits give a method number for method values.\nIf flag.kind() != Func, code can assume that flagMethod is unset.\n"} flag))

;; A method value represents a curried method invocation
;; like r.Read for some receiver r. The typ+val+flag bits describe
;; the receiver r, but the flag's Kind bits say Func (methods are
;; functions), and the top bits of the flag give the method number
;; in r's type's method table.


(go/type flag uintptr)

(go/const
  ^{:line 71} [^{:val 5} flagKindWidth 5] ; there are 27 kinds
  ^{:line 72} [^{:tag flag :val 31} flagKindMask (- (<< 1 flagKindWidth) 1)]
  ^{:line 73} [^{:tag flag :val 32} flagStickyRO (<< 1 5)]
  ^{:line 74} [^{:tag flag :val 64} flagEmbedRO (<< 1 6)]
  ^{:line 75} [^{:tag flag :val 128} flagIndir (<< 1 7)]
  ^{:line 76} [^{:tag flag :val 256} flagAddr (<< 1 8)]
  ^{:line 77} [^{:tag flag :val 512} flagMethod (<< 1 9)]
  ^{:line 78} [^{:val 10} flagMethodShift 10]
  ^{:line 79} [^{:tag flag :val 96} flagRO (bit-or flagStickyRO flagEmbedRO)])


